<subsection xml:id="sec-18-master-index-subsec-index-learning-path-foundations">
<title>Suggested Learning Path: Foundations</title>
<p>A general foundational progression is:</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\text{Arithmetic}
\rightarrow
\text{Sets}
\rightarrow
\text{Functions}
\rightarrow
\text{Logic}
\rightarrow
\text{Proof}
}</md>
</p>

<p>followed by</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\text{Algebra}
\rightarrow
\text{Calculus}
\rightarrow
\text{Linear Algebra}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-18-master-index-subsec-index-learning-path-pure">
<title>Suggested Learning Path: Pure Mathematics</title>
<p>A possible pure-mathematics progression is</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\text{Foundations}
\rightarrow
\text{Algebra}
\rightarrow
\text{Analysis}
\rightarrow
\text{Topology}
}</md>
</p>

<p>with branches into</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\text{Number Theory},
\quad
\text{Geometry},
\quad
\text{Abstract Algebra},
\quad
\text{Logic}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-18-master-index-subsec-index-learning-path-applied">
<title>Suggested Learning Path: Applied Mathematics</title>
<p>A common applied progression is</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\text{Calculus}
\rightarrow
\text{Linear Algebra}
\rightarrow
\text{Differential Equations}
}</md>
</p>

<p>followed by</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\text{Probability},
\quad
\text{Statistics},
\quad
\text{Optimization},
\quad
\text{Numerical Mathematics}.
}</md>
</p>

<p>These support the applied topics in Chapter 13.</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-18-master-index-subsec-index-learning-path-statistics">
<title>Suggested Learning Path: Data and Statistics</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
\text{Probability}
\rightarrow
\text{Descriptive Statistics}
\rightarrow
\text{Estimation}
\rightarrow
\text{Inference}
}</md>
</p>

<p>followed by</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\text{Regression}
\rightarrow
\text{Multivariate Statistics}
\rightarrow
\text{Statistical Learning}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-18-master-index-subsec-index-learning-path-computation">
<title>Suggested Learning Path: Computation</title>
<p>
<md>\boxed{
\text{Algebra}
\rightarrow
\text{Linear Algebra}
\rightarrow
\text{Calculus}
\rightarrow
\text{Algorithms}
}</md>
</p>

<p>followed by</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\text{Numerical Analysis}
\rightarrow
\text{Scientific Computing}
\rightarrow
\text{Simulation}.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-18-master-index-subsec-index-learning-path-modeling">
<title>Suggested Learning Path: Mathematical Modeling</title>
<p>A modeling workflow draws from several subjects:</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\text{Problem Definition}
\rightarrow
\text{Variables and Parameters}
\rightarrow
\text{Assumptions}
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\rightarrow
\text{Mathematical Model}
\rightarrow
\text{Analysis}
\rightarrow
\text{Computation}
}</md>
</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
\rightarrow
\text{Calibration}
\rightarrow
\text{Validation}
\rightarrow
\text{Interpretation}.
}</md>
</p>

<p>Relevant chapters include:</p>

<p>
<md>\boxed{
5,\ 7,\ 8,\ 9,\ 10,\ 11,\ 13.
}</md>
</p>
</subsection>

<subsection xml:id="sec-18-master-index-subsec-index-cross-disciplinary-connections">
<title>Cross-Disciplinary Connections</title>
<p>Many major topics connect several branches simultaneously.</p>

<p>For example:</p>

<p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><em>Fourier analysis</em>
    connects Analysis, Differential Equations, Numerical Mathematics,
    Physics, and Signal Models.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><em>Eigenvalues</em>
    connect Linear Algebra, Differential Equations, Stability,
    Network Science, Statistics, and Quantum Mechanics.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><em>Optimization</em>
    connects Calculus, Linear Algebra, Statistics, Economics,
    Control Theory, and Operations Research.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><em>Probability</em>
    connects Statistics, Stochastic Processes, Finance, Biology,
    Queueing, and Statistical Mechanics.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><em>Graph theory</em>
    connects Combinatorics, Algorithms, Optimization, Networks,
    Biology, and Social Systems.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><em>Differential geometry</em>
    connects Geometry, Topology, Mechanics, Relativity,
    and Geometric Analysis.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><em>Number theory</em>
    connects Algebra, Geometry, Complex Analysis, and Cryptography.</p>
</li>
</ul>
</p>
</subsection>

